A||N||13||bHooper||I GOT TO DRIVE A NORTHSTAR FIERO!!!!!||||1||
Z||000000||bHooper||04-21-2001||04:38 PM||||teeheehehehehhheeee!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>IM AS HAPPY AS A YOUNG GIRL!<P>In fact, everyone that showed up to the NC fiero Group meeting, and chose to, got to ride in and drive Bryan Wilkinson's new Northstar powered '88 GT!<P>WOW!<P>The best part is, Bryan let my fiance' take if for a drive... <B>and she liked it!</B>... so maybe, just maybe, there will be an authorization for me to do a v-8 powered car, in the future!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Thanks a bunch for the ride, and letting me drive it, Bryan!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's<BR>and spellcheck crash's windows<BR>Poly Bushings<BR>Accel Coil||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||04-21-2001||04:57 PM||||Lucky you!!  I have been contemplating a Northstar for about a year now (ever since I visited Design One in OKC).<P>How did it feel?  Handle?  Give us some details.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||04-21-2001||05:06 PM||||.... I can't stop droooling all over myself!<P>Guys... this was incredible!  The first time, Bryan took me for a spin up the highway, it was jsut an amazing feeling.  We hit 100 mph, without any struggle, heck, if you weren't looking at the speedo, you would've thought we were doing 60!<P>he then took Melinda for a drive, and let here drive back... so he had to let me drive it then, WOW!  The car has soooo much power, I can't describe it.  It was an amazing feeling!  In fact, the car would even lose traction a bit, when you let off the throttle!  Bryan is hoping that switching to bigger tires will fix that.<P>But let me say, that that was an incredible ride!  Unfortunatly, he is going to the swap meet, or I would get him to go up to VIR for the Ferrari challenge, next weekend, and do touring laps afterwards!<P>AMAZING!  <P>I need to go lay down, now.<P>hoop<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||04-21-2001||05:07 PM||||Man!  You wasted not time in getting back on the forum.  Of course, YOU didn't have to drive back to Raleigh!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  <P>It was a great meeting.  The Northstar was awesome, and I loved checking out all the other nice Fieros, too (can you say chrome?).  <P>Do you remember what brand wheels were on Bryan's N*?  I thought he said Ronal, but I apparently heard wrong.  That or my memory went with the hair when I shaved my head.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ciao!<BR>John ||||reg||10
Z||000004||Formula88||04-21-2001||05:09 PM||||Nevermind about the wheels.  I found them.  I was looking for <A HREF="http://www.ronalwheels.com" TARGET=_blank>www.ronalwheels.com</A>  and the site was <A HREF="http://www.ronalusa.com." TARGET=_blank>www.ronalusa.com.</A>   My bad.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Bob Englert||04-21-2001||11:29 PM||||I also got to drive Bryan's Northstar Fiero.  3 words - Oh My God!!!<P>I have decided that I cannot own a car like that, I would either be dead or in jail!  Seriously, I don't think I have ever ridden or driven a car that was as much fun as this.  I hit 84 at the end of the merge ramp onto I-40 without really trying hard.  80-90 feels like 60 the engine is so smooth behind you.<P>Thanks again Bryan for the opportunity.  I look forward to seeing the body and interior come together over the next several months.<P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||04-21-2001||11:51 PM||||I remeber last years michigan show , Chris Moore took me out in his 87 GT N*. The power was amazing , reminded me of our 911 RSR ...very progressive flat torque curve..had power all over the rev range...I guess it pays to have 4 cams.. Smooth and docile when it needed to be , an absolute monster when the power was put down.  I was amazed at the cars manners in traffic , the technological advancement of the engine was quite apperent..and a sound that is hard to describe.<P>Hats off to anyone who has done this conversion , it's simply outstanding.<P><BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 2.8 with power nothing short of Crap- tac-ular.||||reg||1
